{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-95113e17acf7771c", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# NVMOS: Non-Verbal Vocalization Quality Assessment in Speech\narXiv: 2606.15888\nAuthors: Jialong Mai, Jinxin Ji, Xiaofen Xing, Wencui Liu, Xiangmin Xu\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n===\n# MiMo-Audio: Audio Language Models are Few-Shot Learners\narXiv: 2512.23808\nAuthors: Xiaomi LLM-Core Team, :, Dong Zhang, Gang Wang, Jinlong Xue, Kai Fang, Liang Zhao, Rui Ma, Shuhuai Ren, Shuo Liu, Tao Guo, Weiji Zhuang, Xin Zhang, Xingchen Song, Yihan Yan, Yongzhe He, Cici, Bowen Shen, Chengxuan Zhu, Chong Ma, Chun Chen, Heyu Chen, Jiawei Li, Lei Li, Menghang Zhu, Peidian Li, Qiying Wang, Sirui Deng, Weimin Xiong, Wenshan Huang, Wenyu Yang, Yilin Jiang, Yixin Yang, Yuanyuan Tian, Yue Ma, Yue Yu, Zihan Zhang, Zihao Yue, Bangjun Xiao, Bingquan Xia, Bofei Gao, Bowen Ye, Can Cai, Chang Liu, Chenhong He, Chunan Li, Dawei Zhu, Duo Zhang, Fengyuan Shi, Guoan Wang, Hailin Zhang, Hanglong Lv, Hanyu Li, Hao Tian, Heng Qu, Hongshen Xu, Houbin Zhang, Huaqiu Liu, Jiangshan Duo, Jianguang Zuo, Jianyu Wei, Jiebao Xiao, Jinhao Dong, Jun Shi, Junhao Hu, Kainan Bao, Kang Zhou, Linghao Zhang, Meng Chen, Nuo Chen, Peng Zhang, Qianli Chen, Qiantong Wang, Rang Li, Shaohui Liu, Shengfan Wang, Shicheng Li, Shihua Yu, Shijie Cao, Shimao Chen, Shuhao Gu, Weikun Wang, Wenhan Ma, Xiangwei Deng, Xing Yong, Xing Zhang, Xu Wang, Yifan Song, Yihao Zhao, Yingbo Zhao, Yizhao Gao, Yu Cheng, Yu Tu, Yudong Wang, Zhaojun Huang, Zhengju Tang, Zhenru Lin, Zhichao Song, Zhipeng Xu, Zhixian Zheng, Zihan Jiang\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We present the first empirical evidence that scaling lossless, compression-based speech pre-training to an unprecedented 100 million hours unlocks emergent task generalization, exemplified by powerful few-shot learning abilities.\n  2. We propose the first comprehensive and replicable blueprint for generative speech pre-training, which includes a novel tokenizer, a scalable architecture, a phased training strategy, and a holistic evaluation suite.\n  3. We pioneer the integration of thinking into the modeling process for both speech understanding and generation, bridging the gap between perception and complex cognitive tasks.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/音频标记-融合, LALM/理解型, 压缩, 压缩/量化-RVQ\n===\n# Neural networks for Text-to-Speech evaluation\narXiv: 2604.08562\nAuthors: Ilya Trofimenko, David Kocharyan, Aleksandr Zaitsev, Pavel Repnikov, Mark Levin, Nikita Shevtsov\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_other\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of a collaborative-filtering-inspired data standardization method (Std SOMOS) that mitigates rater bias and consistently improves absolute MOS prediction accuracy.\n  2. Development of NeuralSBS, a HuBERT-backed model with antisymmetric bilinear pooling that achieves 73.7% accuracy for relative side-by-side TTS evaluation.\n  3. Optimization of the MOSNet architecture through custom sequence-length batching, padding masking, and sequence-level MSE loss to stabilize training and reduce prediction error.\n  4. Proposal of WhisperBert, a multimodal stacking ensemble combining Whisper audio features and BERT text embeddings via weak learners, which achieves an RMSE of ~0.40, significantly outperforming the human inter-rater baseline.\n  5. Demonstration that naive multimodal fusion via cross-attention degrades performance, whereas late-stage ensemble stacking effectively leverages both audio and text modalities.\n  6. Reporting of negative results for SpeechLM-based architectures and zero-shot LLM evaluators, highlighting the necessity of dedicated metric learning frameworks over general-purpose models.\n\nTags: Eval, Eval/学习, TTS\n===\n# FireRedTTS-2: Towards Long Conversational Speech Generation for Podcast and Chatbot\narXiv: 2509.02020\nAuthors: Kun Xie, Feiyu Shen, Junjie Li, Fenglong Xie, Xu Tang, Yao Hu\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A new 12.5Hz streaming speech tokenizer that accelerates training and inference, extends maximum dialogue length, encodes richer semantics for stable modeling, and supports high-fidelity streaming generation.\n  2. A dual-transformer text-to-speech model that operates on text-speech interleaved sequences to enable flexible sentence-by-sentence generation and significantly reduce first-packet latency.\n  3. Seamless integration into interactive chat frameworks, enabling the model to produce emotionally expressive speech guided by implicit contextual cues with minimal fine-tuning.\n  4. Superior zero-shot podcast generation performance, outperforming existing state-of-the-art dialogue systems in objective intelligibility, speaker-turn reliability, and contextually coherent prosody.\n  5. The ability to be rapidly tailored to specific podcast speakers with minimal data, generating dialogue speech that is indistinguishable from human recordings in over half of subjective evaluations.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-流式, TTS/功能-多说话人, TTS/功能-长时间, 压缩", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "3483c3dd-35ce-4c18-9530-2fe55290a039", "uuid": "8a666a06-1095-4d26-865c-ba9cc67ab792", "timestamp": "2026-08-04T11:56:13.161Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# NVMOS: Non-Verbal Vocalization Quality Assessment in Speech\narXiv: 2606.15888\nAuthors: Jialong Mai, Jinxin Ji, Xiaofen Xing, Wencui Liu, Xiangmin Xu\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n===\n# MiMo-Audio: Audio Language Models are Few-Shot Learners\narXiv: 2512.23808\nAuthors: Xiaomi LLM-Core Team, :, Dong Zhang, Gang Wang, Jinlong Xue, Kai Fang, Liang Zhao, Rui Ma, Shuhuai Ren, Shuo Liu, Tao Guo, Weiji Zhuang, Xin Zhang, Xingchen Song, Yihan Yan, Yongzhe He, Cici, Bowen Shen, Chengxuan Zhu, Chong Ma, Chun Chen, Heyu Chen, Jiawei Li, Lei Li, Menghang Zhu, Peidian Li, Qiying Wang, Sirui Deng, Weimin Xiong, Wenshan Huang, Wenyu Yang, Yilin Jiang, Yixin Yang, Yuanyuan Tian, Yue Ma, Yue Yu, Zihan Zhang, Zihao Yue, Bangjun Xiao, Bingquan Xia, Bofei Gao, Bowen Ye, Can Cai, Chang Liu, Chenhong He, Chunan Li, Dawei Zhu, Duo Zhang, Fengyuan Shi, Guoan Wang, Hailin Zhang, Hanglong Lv, Hanyu Li, Hao Tian, Heng Qu, Hongshen Xu, Houbin Zhang, Huaqiu Liu, Jiangshan Duo, Jianguang Zuo, Jianyu Wei, Jiebao Xiao, Jinhao Dong, Jun Shi, Junhao Hu, Kainan Bao, Kang Zhou, Linghao Zhang, Meng Chen, Nuo Chen, Peng Zhang, Qianli Chen, Qiantong Wang, Rang Li, Shaohui Liu, Shengfan Wang, Shicheng Li, Shihua Yu, Shijie Cao, Shimao Chen, Shuhao Gu, Weikun Wang, Wenhan Ma, Xiangwei Deng, Xing Yong, Xing Zhang, Xu Wang, Yifan Song, Yihao Zhao, Yingbo Zhao, Yizhao Gao, Yu Cheng, Yu Tu, Yudong Wang, Zhaojun Huang, Zhengju Tang, Zhenru Lin, Zhichao Song, Zhipeng Xu, Zhixian Zheng, Zihan Jiang\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We present the first empirical evidence that scaling lossless, compression-based speech pre-training to an unprecedented 100 million hours unlocks emergent task generalization, exemplified by powerful few-shot learning abilities.\n  2. We propose the first comprehensive and replicable blueprint for generative speech pre-training, which includes a novel tokenizer, a scalable architecture, a phased training strategy, and a holistic evaluation suite.\n  3. We pioneer the integration of thinking into the modeling process for both speech understanding and generation, bridging the gap between perception and complex cognitive tasks.\n\nTags: LALM, LALM/音频标记-融合, LALM/理解型, 压缩, 压缩/量化-RVQ\n===\n# Neural networks for Text-to-Speech evaluation\narXiv: 2604.08562\nAuthors: Ilya Trofimenko, David Kocharyan, Aleksandr Zaitsev, Pavel Repnikov, Mark Levin, Nikita Shevtsov\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: speech_other\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of a collaborative-filtering-inspired data standardization method (Std SOMOS) that mitigates rater bias and consistently improves absolute MOS prediction accuracy.\n  2. Development of NeuralSBS, a HuBERT-backed model with antisymmetric bilinear pooling that achieves 73.7% accuracy for relative side-by-side TTS evaluation.\n  3. Optimization of the MOSNet architecture through custom sequence-length batching, padding masking, and sequence-level MSE loss to stabilize training and reduce prediction error.\n  4. Proposal of WhisperBert, a multimodal stacking ensemble combining Whisper audio features and BERT text embeddings via weak learners, which achieves an RMSE of ~0.40, significantly outperforming the human inter-rater baseline.\n  5. Demonstration that naive multimodal fusion via cross-attention degrades performance, whereas late-stage ensemble stacking effectively leverages both audio and text modalities.\n  6. Reporting of negative results for SpeechLM-based architectures and zero-shot LLM evaluators, highlighting the necessity of dedicated metric learning frameworks over general-purpose models.\n\nTags: Eval, Eval/学习, TTS\n===\n# FireRedTTS-2: Towards Long Conversational Speech Generation for Podcast and Chatbot\narXiv: 2509.02020\nAuthors: Kun Xie, Feiyu Shen, Junjie Li, Fenglong Xie, Xu Tang, Yao Hu\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. A new 12.5Hz streaming speech tokenizer that accelerates training and inference, extends maximum dialogue length, encodes richer semantics for stable modeling, and supports high-fidelity streaming generation.\n  2. A dual-transformer text-to-speech model that operates on text-speech interleaved sequences to enable flexible sentence-by-sentence generation and significantly reduce first-packet latency.\n  3. Seamless integration into interactive chat frameworks, enabling the model to produce emotionally expressive speech guided by implicit contextual cues with minimal fine-tuning.\n  4. Superior zero-shot podcast generation performance, outperforming existing state-of-the-art dialogue systems in objective intelligibility, speaker-turn reliability, and contextually coherent prosody.\n  5. The ability to be rapidly tailored to specific podcast speakers with minimal data, generating dialogue speech that is indistinguishable from human recordings in over half of subjective evaluations.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/功能-流式, TTS/功能-多说话人, TTS/功能-长时间, 压缩", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
